  "kind": "recipe",
  "metadata": {
    "alignment": "unspecified",
    "description": "Installable Candidate reproducing MiaAI-Lab's public 6f7d1590 kit (release 2026-09-19, no upstream version tag) on the digest-pinned vllm/vllm-openai:deepseekv41-flash-0909 arm64 image, the only base carrying the DeepseekV41 architecture: the 196 GiB Mia-AiLab EXL3 2.9 bpw checkpoint at 64ba41b6, tensor-parallel 2 over the Spark fabric, native DSpark (k=3), file-backed Engram tables read from shards 47 and 48 of the official deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash checkpoint (dba1be0a, declared as a second Model, about 189 GiB per node), 600k context, 2 sequences, a 2.5 GiB pinned KV pool, vision input and tools. Chosen over sfxnz's 3de91468 kit (MIT, 2.0 bpw pack, claims 39.6 tok/s greedy) because it is a single self-contained Dockerfile, the higher-quality 2.9 bpw pack and the closest sibling of the existing Mia EXL3 recipe; sfxnz's kit needs a chain of patch images, a 334 GB pack and further first-use kernel compilation. The kit source is AGPL-3.0 with earlier MIT contributions (upstream-LICENSE, upstream-LICENSE-MIT); both Models are MIT. Upstream claims (not measured here): about 23 to 39 tok/s single stream depending on workload, 774,400-token KV pool, and a first boot of about 25 minutes. Not exposed: the cooperative-MoE binary (needs an unpinned prebuilt library), Engram row packing (a host-side artifact), the language-model-only switch, the memory-guard watchdog and the third-party abliterated overlay. The engine-ready timeout is 3600 s (upstream 1500 s) because upstream reports a first boot of about 25 minutes. Thinking is on by default (reasoning effort high), so a small max_tokens can return empty content unless chat_template_kwargs.enable_thinking is false. Vonk physical acceptance is pending.",
